; AlifePlus outpost stock policy. Filters a conquered-area service NPC's player-facing stock after each restock, so a field outpost sells a lean assortment, not the full faction
; shelf. Applied on top of the below-hub supplies drop (Mutators > Conquest): this file decides which kinds a service stocks, the supplies drop decides how deep its ammo/gear tiers go.
; DLTX-overridable.
;
; One block per service role. A cap that suits a trader guts a specialist (a barman's trade is food and drink, a medic's is medical, a mechanic's is tools and parts), so each role is
; capped generously in its own trade and hard everywhere else and stays recognisably itself. A role whose block is missing or empty is not filtered (logged at load).
;
; Format: key = N, a cap; there is no minimum (nothing here adds stock, it only removes over the cap). N = 0 strips the kind from stock; a deleted row leaves that category untouched.
; A key counts by its name. A category is a shelf total for the whole category (food = 8 is 8 food items of all kinds, the only cap that keeps a 77-section supply list lean). An ammo
; category is rounds per type, not boxes (90 = 90 rounds of each type; a box counts as its rounds, and a value below one box size strips that ammo since stacks release whole). A single
; item section caps that section alone and overrides its category (energy_drink = 2). money is the role's bankroll in rubles, reset on every restock, so sell-to-cash is capped per cycle;
; a deleted money row leaves his cash to the engine. Category names match get_section_category. Equipped weapon, armor, and quest items are never in scope; the categorizer skips them.

; Field resupply post: ammo by the caseload plus a little of everything else.
[ap_outpost_stock_trader]
money                = 10000
ammo_rounds_per_type = 60
grenade_ammo         = 2
grenade              = 2
medkit               = 2
bandage              = 4
antirad              = 2
stim                 = 2
pill                 = 2
food                 = 5
drink                = 4
crafting             = 4
weapon               = 0
outfit               = 0
helmet               = 0
artefact             = 0
device               = 0
other                = 0

